    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive profile, anchored by **Junior Caminero** (78.48) and **Yordan Alvarez** (78.37), both of whom offer the highest daily efficiency scores due to favorable park factors and high-impact batting order positions. **Junior Caminero** in particular benefits from a substantial +14% park adjustment, making him our primary engine against Hughes. We are also leaning heavily on the top-of-the-order dynamism of **Kyle Schwarber** (77.87) and **Trea Turner** (77.46); their matchup against the left-handed Palmquist presents an ideal environment for exploitation, with each player carrying significant weight from their placement in the two-hole and leadoff spots, respectively.\n\nWhile **Lars Nootbaar** (65.16) offers a strong return on investment thanks to an elite +19% SP skill adjustment against the vulnerable V\u00e1squez, the most complex decision involved our bench depth. **Carson Benge** (47.25) was the strongest candidate for promotion, but he ultimately remained benched due to a significant -9% platoon disadvantage against Cantillo. Similarly, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (46.66) possesses the elite sprint speed we covet to bolster our scarce SB category, the overwhelming risk posed by facing an elite arm like Skubal (2.67 xERA) and a prohibitive -15% platoon penalty forced him to the pine. We are monitoring the status of **Dillon Dingler**, who fell below our 40.0 efficiency floor, alongside **Gary Sanchez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**, all of whom remain out of the primary tactical calculation for today's rotation. With no immediate weather threats, we look to **Colt Keith** (50.95) and **Nelson Velazquez** (48.04) to provide the necessary floor to protect our category standings.",
